{
  "dom_id": "step-q142968",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y\\le 1).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}[{2}^{4}-{0}^{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le 1) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,{y}^{1/3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{2}}{[\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{4/3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[3]{2}}[{1}^{4/3}-{0}^{4/3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[3]{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
